---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Background, how I work, and what I'm building toward."
>
  <section class="wrap py-20">
    <h1 class="text-[clamp(2.25rem,5vw,3.5rem)]">About</h1>

    {/* TODO: everything below is placeholder shaped correctly. Rewrite in your voice. */}
    <div class="prose-measure mt-10 space-y-6 text-lg text-ink-muted">
      <p>
        I&rsquo;m an engineer who builds and ships products end to end — the research, the
        architecture, the interface, and the part where it goes live and has to stay up.
      </p>
      <p>
        Lately most of my work has been AI-powered products: systems where a model does something
        genuinely useful inside a product that a non-technical person can actually operate. That
        second half is where most of these projects fail, and it&rsquo;s the half I care about.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal mt-20 grid gap-12 rounded-2xl bg-surface-alt p-8 md:grid-cols-[1fr_1.4fr] sm:p-12">
      <h2 class="font-display text-[clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem)]">How I work</h2>
      <div class="space-y-5 text-ink-muted">
        <p>
          <strong class="text-ink">Ship the smallest real version first.</strong> Most projects that
          sound like they need a large system need a smaller one in front of users sooner. Real
          usage answers questions that planning cannot.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-ink">Own the whole thing.</strong> Fewer handoffs, fewer things lost
          between them. I&rsquo;d rather be responsible for the outcome than for one layer of it.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-ink">Build for the person who isn&rsquo;t technical.</strong> If the
          person who needs the tool can&rsquo;t run it without me, it isn&rsquo;t finished.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal mt-20 grid gap-12 border-t border-line pt-14 md:grid-cols-[1fr_1.4fr]">
      <h2 class="font-display text-[clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem)]">What I&rsquo;m building toward</h2>
      <div class="space-y-5 text-ink-muted">
        <p>
          {/* TODO: this is the most personal section on the site. Worth writing yourself. */}
          I&rsquo;m building my own products and taking on a small number of client projects
          alongside them. The goal is a small portfolio of things I own outright, funded by work
          I&rsquo;m glad to do.
        </p>
        <a href="mailto:tanner.kunz22@gmail.com" class="link-wipe inline-block text-primary">
          Get in touch
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
